<%- include('../partials/header') %>

<div class="page-head">
  <h1>Download your data</h1>
  <p class="sub">
    Everything this parish has entered, in a form you can keep, print from or
    take to another system. The records are yours; this page is how you get a
    copy of them without asking anyone.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="stats" style="margin-bottom:22px">
  <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= stats.families %></div><div class="k">Families</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= stats.members %></div><div class="k">People</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= photos %></div><div class="k">Photographs</div></div>
  <div class="stat">
    <div class="n"><%= stats.families - stats.published %></div>
    <div class="k">Drafts, not printed</div>
  </div>
</div>

<form method="get" action="<%= base %>/admin/export.zip" class="card" id="download-form">
  <h2>What to include</h2>

  <div class="field">
    <label>
      <input type="checkbox" name="drafts" value="0" id="skip-drafts">
      Leave out drafts &mdash; only the
      <strong><%= stats.published %></strong> entries that go into the printed book
    </label>
    <p class="help">
      Drafts are included by default. Leave them in for a copy you are keeping;
      take them out for a copy you are handing to a printer.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="actions">
    <button type="submit" class="btn">Spreadsheet and photographs (.zip)</button>
    <button type="submit" class="btn ghost" formaction="<%= base %>/admin/export.csv">
      Spreadsheet only (.csv)
    </button>
  </div>

  <p class="help">
    The archive holds <code>families.csv</code> and a <code>photos</code>
    folder. Each photograph is named after the family it belongs to, and the
    last column of the spreadsheet gives that name &mdash; so a row and a face
    can be matched without opening the application.
  </p>
</form>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Before you send it anywhere</h2>
  <p class="help" style="margin-top:0">
    This file is every address, telephone number and date of birth in the
    parish, together with the photographs. It carries no password of any kind.
    Treat it the way the parish would treat the printed directory before it is
    handed out &mdash; and delete the copy in your downloads folder once it has
    reached wherever it was going.
  </p>
  <p class="help">
    The spreadsheet has one row per person, with the family&rsquo;s details
    repeated on each of their rows. That is the shape that sorts and filters in
    Excel; a file with one row per family cannot hold the members at all.
  </p>
  <p class="help">
    A download of a few thousand photographs takes minutes and runs to hundreds
    of megabytes. It starts immediately and nothing is stored on the server
    while it runs &mdash; but if the browser looks idle, it is still working.
    Clicking again starts a second one.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
